James inquired about translating a `dplyr` code snippet from R to Julia and executing an R script within Julia. I provided a method using the `DataFrames` and `DataFramesMeta` packages, demonstrating how to group and summarize a DataFrame. James then faced an error when loading the `RCall` package, which prompted a discussion on setting the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`. Despite following the suggested steps and confirming the path, the error persisted. I recommended checking R installation, trying `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH`, launching Julia directly from the terminal, reinstalling R if necessary, and provided an alternative approach to run R scripts using `run()`.
